  "id": "sensory-suppression",
  "term": "sensory suppression",
  "definition": "Sensory suppression is a biological process in which the nervous system reduces selected incoming sensory information. In the source packet, it is described as a form of sensory inhibition seen when the response to a second identical auditory or somatosensory stimulus is weaker than the response to the first.",
